    "title": "pandas.PeriodIndex.freqstr — pandas 2.2.3 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.PeriodIndex.freqstr#\n\n- \n*property* PeriodIndex.freqstr[source]#\n- Return the frequency object as a string if it’s set, otherwise None. Examples For DatetimeIndex: >>> idx = pd.DatetimeIndex([\"1/1/2020 10:00:00+00:00\"], freq=\"D\") >>> idx.freqstr 'D' The frequency can be inferred if there are more than 2 points: >>> idx = pd.DatetimeIndex([\"2018-01-01\", \"2018-01-03\", \"2018-01-05\"], ... freq=\"infer\") >>> idx.freqstr '2D' For PeriodIndex: >>> idx = pd.PeriodIndex([\"2023-1\", \"2023-2\", \"2023-3\"], freq=\"M\") >>> idx.freqstr 'M'",
    "markdown_length": 535,
